# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Env layering (env files cannot import each other — we load them in order):
#   real OS/runtime env  >  .env (this file — personal, gitignored,
#                           one per workspace)  >  .env.shared (local,
#                           gitignored)  >  ../MarkBrain/.env.markbrain-main.shared
#                           (canonical credentials shared by all worktrees;
#                           fills only keys not already set — see server.ts)
#
# RULE: env files NEVER enter git. Only this .example template is tracked,
# and it holds placeholders only.
#
# Only put values you need to OVERRIDE per workspace here — often just:
#   PORT=3093
# Non-secret defaults can live in .env.shared (also gitignored).
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# GEMINI_API_KEY: Required for Gemini AI API calls.
# AI Studio automatically injects this at runtime from user secrets.
# Users configure this via the Secrets panel in the AI Studio UI.
GEMINI_API_KEY="MY_GEMINI_API_KEY"

# APP_URL: The URL where this applet is hosted.
# AI Studio automatically injects this at runtime with the Cloud Run service URL.
# Used for self-referential links, OAuth callbacks, and API endpoints.
APP_URL="MY_APP_URL"

# No cloud-auth variables. Firebase, Firestore, and Google Drive were removed
# (design-docs/19). The VPS account system (Phase 2) reads MARKBRAIN_OWNER_EMAIL
# / MARKBRAIN_OWNER_PASSWORD from the server env, never from this template.
